    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Juniperus navicularis</b></i> (syn. <b><i>Juniperus oxycedrus</i> subsp. <i>transtagana</i></b>), the <b>Portuguese prickly juniper</b>, is a species of juniper endemic to the southwestern Iberian Peninsula. Although it is sometimes considered a subspecies of the Mediterranean <i>Juniperus oxycedrus</i>, phylogenetic studies have found the two are not closely related.",
